1
00:00:28,528 --> 00:00:29,946
TAKE CHARGE OF MY HEART

2
00:00:31,322 --> 00:00:32,824
Do you know Bo-bae?

3
00:00:32,907 --> 00:00:34,242
Of course I do.

4
00:00:34,325 --> 00:00:35,410
I am

5
00:00:36,077 --> 00:00:37,746
a huge fan

6
00:00:38,413 --> 00:00:39,831
of Ms. Na Bo-bae, you see.

7
00:00:46,087 --> 00:00:46,921
Ms. Na.

8
00:00:48,298 --> 00:00:49,966
What brings you here?

9
00:00:50,050 --> 00:00:51,259
Hello, sir.

10
00:00:51,342 --> 00:00:52,260
Yeah.

11
00:00:55,889 --> 00:00:57,265
Oh!

12
00:00:58,099 --> 00:01:01,227
You said you were working
on a new project with Director Yeom.

13
00:01:01,811 --> 00:01:05,148
That's the drama Mr. Baek's been talking
to you about sponsoring?

14
00:01:05,231 --> 00:01:07,067
Huh? Sponsoring?

15
00:01:08,318 --> 00:01:09,736
-Well…
-Director.

16
00:01:09,819 --> 00:01:12,781
I heard Ji Eun-ho got cast
in Bo-bae's drama.

17
00:01:12,864 --> 00:01:14,407
What are you talking about?

18
00:01:14,491 --> 00:01:17,494
Ji Eun-ho's been cast in the drama
Ms. Na and I are working on?

19
00:01:18,328 --> 00:01:21,414
She must've told you
what she was hoping for.

20
00:01:21,998 --> 00:01:22,832
Was that it?

21
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:26,753
Oh dear. I must've misunderstood.

22
00:01:27,837 --> 00:01:30,173
Bo-bae, you told me the other day.

23
00:01:30,256 --> 00:01:33,676
That the director was raving
about your script,

24
00:01:33,760 --> 00:01:35,887
and Ji Eun-ho had the male lead.

25
00:01:38,932 --> 00:01:42,102
I see. She said I was raving?

26
00:01:42,185 --> 00:01:44,395
Yeah, I sure was.

27
00:01:44,479 --> 00:01:46,147
Raving, all right.

28
00:01:46,231 --> 00:01:48,900
But really, Ms. Na's scripts
are much better these days.

29
00:01:48,983 --> 00:01:51,027
Yeah, they're really great.

30
00:01:51,111 --> 00:01:51,945
Well…

31
00:01:52,946 --> 00:01:54,280
I'm sorry.

32
00:01:54,364 --> 00:01:57,867
I tend to get carried away when I talk.

33
00:01:57,951 --> 00:02:00,161
No, it's fine. I get it.

34
00:02:00,245 --> 00:02:01,704
You need a little swagger.

35
00:02:01,788 --> 00:02:04,582
Otherwise, you can't hold your own
in this industry.

36
00:02:04,666 --> 00:02:05,500
It's fine.

37
00:02:05,583 --> 00:02:06,793
What?

38
00:02:07,293 --> 00:02:09,003
Did you lie to me?

39
00:02:13,424 --> 00:02:17,303
Mr. Baek, that's what we writers do.

40
00:02:17,387 --> 00:02:19,931
We basically make things up.

41
00:02:20,932 --> 00:02:22,809
Don't believe everything Bo-bae says.

42
00:02:25,145 --> 00:02:29,149
Doesn't that make Ms. Na
all the more impressive?

43
00:02:30,650 --> 00:02:31,818
Because I fell

44
00:02:32,861 --> 00:02:34,279
for her story.

45
00:02:43,246 --> 00:02:44,080
Ms. Na.

46
00:02:45,957 --> 00:02:49,169
Shall we take a look
at the resort's penthouse first?

47
00:03:44,724 --> 00:03:46,309
Pull yourself together.

48
00:03:46,392 --> 00:03:48,436
Okay.

49
00:03:48,519 --> 00:03:51,814
Why listen to someone who's clearly
just trying to get under your skin?

50
00:03:51,898 --> 00:03:53,608
I mean, I…

51
00:03:54,525 --> 00:03:56,861
I guess I did talk things up a little.

52
00:03:56,945 --> 00:03:58,655
It was more than just a little.

53
00:03:58,738 --> 00:04:01,032
You went way overboard.

54
00:04:04,577 --> 00:04:05,912
Mr. Baek.

55
00:04:05,995 --> 00:04:06,996
Oh.

56
00:04:08,998 --> 00:04:10,833
I was just leaving a TS ad meeting.

57
00:04:11,668 --> 00:04:13,086
I didn't expect to see you.

58
00:04:13,169 --> 00:04:14,045
Right.

59
00:04:14,837 --> 00:04:16,923
I haven't seen you since my birthday.

60
00:04:17,006 --> 00:04:19,884
I bet a lot of people
have been asking you about us.

61
00:04:19,968 --> 00:04:23,805
After the article, people around me
thought we already set a wedding date.

62
00:04:23,888 --> 00:04:25,431
Actually,

63
00:04:25,515 --> 00:04:27,976
I'd like a word with you about that.

64
00:04:28,059 --> 00:04:30,103
-I don't think we've met.
-Sorry?

65
00:04:30,687 --> 00:04:32,897
Right. I'm his secretary.

66
00:04:32,981 --> 00:04:34,232
My name is Na Bo-bae.

67
00:04:35,149 --> 00:04:36,359
So you're his secretary.

68
00:04:37,694 --> 00:04:39,445
Han Seol-hee, director of Hanlim.

69
00:04:40,029 --> 00:04:41,030
Right.

70
00:04:42,532 --> 00:04:43,366
Yes.

71
00:04:50,665 --> 00:04:55,461
Mr. Baek, shouldn't your secretary leave
if you want to talk to me?

72
00:04:56,045 --> 00:04:58,965
Oh, I'll give you two a moment.

73
00:05:00,550 --> 00:05:02,135
I can say it now.

74
00:05:02,969 --> 00:05:04,804
Just give me three months.

75
00:05:05,596 --> 00:05:07,348
-Three months?
-Yes.

76
00:05:07,932 --> 00:05:11,811
By then, I'll show what kind of leader
I can be for TS.

77
00:05:12,395 --> 00:05:16,482
Then my grandmother won't try to force
this arranged marriage.

78
00:05:16,566 --> 00:05:21,029
You don't want to sacrifice your life
for the company either, do you?

79
00:05:23,489 --> 00:05:25,325
But I do want to marry you.

80
00:05:27,702 --> 00:05:28,703
Sorry?

81
00:05:30,079 --> 00:05:32,040
I guess we need to talk some more.

82
00:05:33,708 --> 00:05:36,753
Ms. Na, could you grab us some coffee?

83
00:05:36,836 --> 00:05:38,087
Decaf for Mr. Baek.

84
00:05:38,671 --> 00:05:41,007
Pay with this.

85
00:05:44,385 --> 00:05:47,388
I can see we're not on the same page.
We can leave it at that.

86
00:05:48,264 --> 00:05:49,682
Well, I have to get going.

87
00:05:49,766 --> 00:05:53,019
And I really need my secretary
with me right now.

88
00:05:53,102 --> 00:05:55,813
I didn't hire her
just to fetch coffee, after all.

89
00:05:56,898 --> 00:05:57,940
I see.

90
00:05:59,776 --> 00:06:01,736
I'm sorry, Ms. Na.

91
00:06:01,819 --> 00:06:04,655
No, it's okay. I can go get it quickly.

92
00:06:05,156 --> 00:06:08,785
I said I need you right now,
Ms. Na Bo-bae.

93
00:06:15,541 --> 00:06:17,001
Make sure you grab a coffee.

94
00:06:17,085 --> 00:06:19,629
Our resort's barista
is a former world champion,

95
00:06:20,213 --> 00:06:22,006
so the coffee's excellent.

96
00:06:22,757 --> 00:06:24,926
I will. See you next time.

97
00:06:25,510 --> 00:06:27,053
Sure. See you next time.

98
00:06:52,120 --> 00:06:55,415
I could tell right away
she's really into you.

99
00:06:55,915 --> 00:06:57,500
Why don't you just marry her?

100
00:06:57,583 --> 00:07:01,546
She's beautiful, capable,
and seems to have a great personality too.

101
00:07:02,046 --> 00:07:04,048
You're getting carried away again.

102
00:07:04,132 --> 00:07:05,174
What was that?

103
00:07:06,968 --> 00:07:08,719
I said I'm not getting married.

104
00:07:08,803 --> 00:07:10,304
And I'm not interested in her.

105
00:07:10,888 --> 00:07:13,015
You should be thanking me, by the way.

106
00:07:13,099 --> 00:07:15,810
I saved you from embarrassing yourself
in front of another writer.

107
00:07:15,893 --> 00:07:17,478
And I saved you a pointless errand.

108
00:07:17,562 --> 00:07:19,480
I never asked you for help.

109
00:07:19,564 --> 00:07:21,941
You did it on your own,
and now you want credit?

110
00:07:22,024 --> 00:07:24,402
Forget it.
Just help me with my bucket list.

111
00:07:24,485 --> 00:07:26,237
Did you forget our contract?

112
00:07:26,320 --> 00:07:28,614
I've been charging you every day,
you know.

113
00:07:28,698 --> 00:07:31,075
Why are you getting so worked up?

114
00:07:31,159 --> 00:07:32,618
I thought you were a chaebol.

115
00:07:32,702 --> 00:07:36,497
Yet you get pushed around by your grandma,
your cousin, and Director Han.

116
00:07:36,581 --> 00:07:39,375
Do you even have any chaebol flex
to show me?

117
00:07:42,170 --> 00:07:43,963
I'll show you some chaebol flex.

118
00:07:44,046 --> 00:07:45,298
What do I have to do?

119
00:07:49,802 --> 00:07:52,388
You rented the whole place?

120
00:07:57,143 --> 00:07:59,812
But how did you manage to…

121
00:07:59,896 --> 00:08:02,398
You asked me to show you
some chaebol flex.

122
00:08:03,483 --> 00:08:08,529
Anyway, how could you have never
been to a theme park? You're almost 30.

123
00:08:08,613 --> 00:08:12,325
Why is this even
on your romance bucket list?

124
00:08:13,451 --> 00:08:17,497
I've been to theme parks before.
Just never with a boyfriend.

125
00:08:18,706 --> 00:08:19,540
Let's go.

126
00:08:21,584 --> 00:08:22,418
Hold on.

127
00:08:22,919 --> 00:08:24,170
What is it now?

128
00:08:24,670 --> 00:08:27,173
If you're at a theme park,
you have to go there.

129
00:08:34,055 --> 00:08:35,014
Come here.

130
00:08:37,391 --> 00:08:40,436
Wearing one of these headbands
is a must at a theme park.

131
00:08:40,520 --> 00:08:44,690
What does wearing a headband have to do
with the romance in your script?

132
00:08:44,774 --> 00:08:48,402
It's the little props that set the mood.

133
00:08:49,153 --> 00:08:50,321
Which one should I wear?

134
00:08:51,322 --> 00:08:53,366
How about this one? So we match.

135
00:08:54,450 --> 00:08:56,494
Hey! The bucket list.

136
00:09:01,040 --> 00:09:02,208
How do I look?

137
00:09:05,253 --> 00:09:07,547
What? They're so cute!

138
00:09:07,630 --> 00:09:09,382
Can we take a picture?

139
00:09:10,591 --> 00:09:11,717
Hi!

140
00:09:13,511 --> 00:09:15,972
Three, two, one.

141
00:09:23,354 --> 00:09:24,855
This is so fun!

142
00:09:44,959 --> 00:09:47,253
Hey, put your hands up!

143
00:09:47,336 --> 00:09:48,879
Put your hands up!

144
00:09:53,718 --> 00:09:56,178
I think I'm going to have a heart attack

145
00:09:56,971 --> 00:09:58,681
before we finish your bucket list.

146
00:09:58,764 --> 00:10:00,474
I'm so sorry.

147
00:10:00,558 --> 00:10:01,392
Are you okay?

148
00:10:02,643 --> 00:10:03,686
You're sweating.

149
00:10:15,823 --> 00:10:18,117
Are you okay?
Shouldn't we go to the hospital?

150
00:10:18,200 --> 00:10:19,285
No!

151
00:10:19,368 --> 00:10:20,453
Well…

152
00:10:20,953 --> 00:10:22,997
You wanted to go to the Haunted House?

153
00:10:23,664 --> 00:10:25,416
Let's go to the Haunted House.

154
00:10:26,000 --> 00:10:27,543
You're obviously not okay.

155
00:10:27,627 --> 00:10:29,795
Your heart rate's over 100.

156
00:10:39,597 --> 00:10:41,349
-Let's go in!
-No.

157
00:10:41,432 --> 00:10:42,642
We can skip this one.

158
00:10:42,725 --> 00:10:44,268
You need to watch your heart.

159
00:10:44,352 --> 00:10:46,646
I don't think
jump scares are good for you.

160
00:10:46,729 --> 00:10:49,440
I don't mind skipping it either.

161
00:10:50,983 --> 00:10:52,193
No. Let's go.

162
00:10:52,276 --> 00:10:53,653
It's on your bucket list.

163
00:10:55,529 --> 00:10:56,614
You think

164
00:10:57,323 --> 00:10:59,116
this scares me?

165
00:11:00,368 --> 00:11:01,619
Wait, Mr. Baek…

166
00:11:02,745 --> 00:11:07,041
The ghosts are real people.
It won't end well if they touch me.

167
00:11:14,256 --> 00:11:15,800
Let's go together.

168
00:11:18,844 --> 00:11:21,597
-What's with you?
-This is…

169
00:11:22,765 --> 00:11:24,183
Damn!

170
00:11:25,935 --> 00:11:27,144
Let's go together.

171
00:11:27,228 --> 00:11:28,896
-You're scared, aren't you?
-No!

172
00:11:33,651 --> 00:11:35,736
My back hurts. Hang on.

173
00:11:39,073 --> 00:11:41,367
That really startled me.

174
00:11:41,867 --> 00:11:44,120
Let's just find the exit
and get out of here.

175
00:11:44,203 --> 00:11:45,413
Right?

176
00:11:45,913 --> 00:11:47,081
I'm totally fine,

177
00:11:47,957 --> 00:11:50,376
but if you insist…

178
00:11:51,752 --> 00:11:52,712
Come on. Let's go.

179
00:11:53,546 --> 00:11:54,672
Let's go together.

180
00:11:58,884 --> 00:12:00,219
What? What is it?

181
00:12:00,302 --> 00:12:03,097
-It's nothing.
-Seriously!

182
00:12:17,611 --> 00:12:19,155
Ms. Na!

183
00:12:19,238 --> 00:12:21,490
-Run! Now!
-Huh?

184
00:12:21,574 --> 00:12:23,284
Hey! Where are you going?

185
00:12:24,076 --> 00:12:25,828
Mr. Baek! Where are you going?

186
00:12:27,747 --> 00:12:28,581
I'm sorry!

187
00:12:29,999 --> 00:12:31,792
Mr. Baek! Wait up!

188
00:12:32,293 --> 00:12:33,169
I'm sorry!

189
00:12:33,753 --> 00:12:34,587
Sorry!

190
00:12:36,839 --> 00:12:39,967
Please stop! I'm sorry, everyone!

191
00:12:50,186 --> 00:12:52,938
What on earth were you doing in there?

192
00:12:53,022 --> 00:12:54,565
How did they end up like that?

193
00:12:55,649 --> 00:12:58,569
You've got some nerve saying that
after running away without me.

194
00:12:59,779 --> 00:13:01,280
I didn't run away.

195
00:13:01,363 --> 00:13:03,282
I thought I was holding your hand!

196
00:13:09,371 --> 00:13:12,208
Either way, how am I supposed to
use this in my script?

197
00:13:12,291 --> 00:13:15,669
A male lead ditching the female lead?
That's asking for a fight.

198
00:13:20,090 --> 00:13:22,218
How's that asking for a fight?

199
00:13:34,730 --> 00:13:35,648
Are you upset?

200
00:13:37,274 --> 00:13:38,359
Like I said earlier,

201
00:13:38,442 --> 00:13:41,821
I didn't mean to leave you behind.
It was an accident.

202
00:13:42,488 --> 00:13:44,031
No, I'm in a good mood.

203
00:13:45,366 --> 00:13:46,909
I'm happy.

204
00:13:50,246 --> 00:13:52,373
Actually, going to a theme park

205
00:13:52,873 --> 00:13:56,669
was more of a life bucket list item
than a romance bucket list one.

206
00:13:57,253 --> 00:14:02,591
I went once when I was a little kid.
I haven't been in almost 20 years.

207
00:14:02,675 --> 00:14:06,262
But today, I got to ride the rides
without anyone else around.

208
00:14:06,345 --> 00:14:08,514
It was nice hanging out with you.

209
00:14:10,057 --> 00:14:12,685
I thought,
"This is what theme parks are like."

210
00:14:12,768 --> 00:14:14,770
"They're so much fun."

211
00:14:15,312 --> 00:14:16,730
"I'm having a blast."

212
00:14:17,565 --> 00:14:20,234
Why did you wait so long?
You could've just gone.

213
00:14:21,944 --> 00:14:22,778
Well,

214
00:14:23,904 --> 00:14:24,780
I was just

215
00:14:25,739 --> 00:14:28,367
a little scared of theme parks.

216
00:14:55,644 --> 00:14:59,440
Anyway, thank you
for going to the theme park with me.

217
00:15:23,047 --> 00:15:25,841
OLD KINDNESS

218
00:15:27,801 --> 00:15:29,345
Hello.

219
00:15:29,428 --> 00:15:30,971
Hello.

220
00:15:32,264 --> 00:15:35,559
You were looking for
a book called Old Kindness, right?

221
00:15:35,643 --> 00:15:37,227
You might find it here.

222
00:15:37,311 --> 00:15:41,565
That'd be great. It's out of print.

223
00:15:53,786 --> 00:15:54,787
It's too…

224
00:16:20,229 --> 00:16:22,523
I guess it was pretty dusty up there.

225
00:16:44,878 --> 00:16:45,713
Bo-bae.

226
00:16:47,715 --> 00:16:48,841
Eun-ho.

227
00:16:48,924 --> 00:16:50,384
What are you doing here?

228
00:16:51,051 --> 00:16:52,219
What's with the headband?

229
00:16:54,805 --> 00:16:57,349
You went to the theme park
with Mr. Baek Ho-rang?

230
00:16:57,433 --> 00:16:59,727
Yes, we did.

231
00:16:59,810 --> 00:17:02,396
It was for research, not for fun.

232
00:17:02,479 --> 00:17:06,025
Sorry. I couldn't check my phone
because I was on the rides.

233
00:17:07,276 --> 00:17:09,653
Huh? What did you want to give me?

234
00:17:09,737 --> 00:17:10,696
Yeah.

235
00:17:12,114 --> 00:17:13,157
Huh? Right.

236
00:17:13,741 --> 00:17:16,243
You said you were stuck on your script
and stressed out.

237
00:17:17,161 --> 00:17:20,039
This is the book you wanted
that was out of print.

238
00:17:20,539 --> 00:17:21,623
I found it for you.

239
00:17:21,707 --> 00:17:22,958
Really?

240
00:17:23,792 --> 00:17:27,129
Eun-ho, you really didn't have to do this.

241
00:17:27,212 --> 00:17:29,465
If I don't, who will?

242
00:17:29,548 --> 00:17:30,632
Eun-ho.

243
00:17:32,968 --> 00:17:34,011
I'm the best, right?

244
00:17:34,094 --> 00:17:35,929
Gosh, don't be silly.

245
00:17:43,687 --> 00:17:45,773
We meet often these days, Mr. Ji Eun-ho.

246
00:17:45,856 --> 00:17:46,940
Indeed.

247
00:17:47,024 --> 00:17:50,611
My team called you dozens of times,
but you never answer.

248
00:17:51,904 --> 00:17:53,405
That has nothing to do with this.

249
00:17:54,156 --> 00:17:56,950
I already declined your offer
to be the face of your resort.

250
00:17:58,869 --> 00:18:00,788
And Bo-bae and I are close.

251
00:18:02,081 --> 00:18:04,208
I'm close with Ms. Na Bo-bae too.

252
00:18:04,291 --> 00:18:05,292
Come on.

253
00:18:06,835 --> 00:18:08,420
Eun-ho, thank you so much.

254
00:18:08,504 --> 00:18:09,463
-I'll enjoy it.
-Yeah.

255
00:18:10,047 --> 00:18:12,257
Call me when you're done.
Tell me what you think.

256
00:18:12,341 --> 00:18:14,593
-Call me.
-Okay. Off you go.

257
00:18:14,676 --> 00:18:15,594
I'll get going.

258
00:18:16,720 --> 00:18:18,514
Wait. Why are you going that way?

259
00:18:25,896 --> 00:18:30,025
It's so dark that I got confused.
It's the one over there.

260
00:18:30,526 --> 00:18:33,070
Mr. Baek, thank you so much for the ride.

261
00:18:33,153 --> 00:18:35,864
I got confused because you parked here.

262
00:18:35,948 --> 00:18:38,408
Good night, Mr. Baek Ho-rang.

263
00:18:38,492 --> 00:18:39,743
What?

264
00:18:40,786 --> 00:18:44,790
Thank you so much for helping me
with my research today.

265
00:18:44,873 --> 00:18:45,958
And thanks, Eun-ho.

266
00:18:46,041 --> 00:18:49,211
-Sure.
-Go on home, both of you.

267
00:18:50,337 --> 00:18:51,505
I'm heading home, then.

268
00:18:51,588 --> 00:18:53,590
You're so silly!

269
00:18:54,341 --> 00:18:57,136
We only met up for research.

270
00:18:57,219 --> 00:18:59,346
Nothing more, nothing less.

271
00:18:59,847 --> 00:19:01,849
It's getting late. You should get going.

272
00:19:01,932 --> 00:19:02,850
Thank you.

273
00:19:03,892 --> 00:19:06,061
-No, but…
-Look.

274
00:19:06,145 --> 00:19:08,730
Are you seriously going
to a woman's house this late?

275
00:19:08,814 --> 00:19:09,857
Mr. Baek?

276
00:19:09,940 --> 00:19:11,191
He's right.

277
00:19:11,275 --> 00:19:13,277
You should go home. To your place.

278
00:19:19,908 --> 00:19:21,285
Sure.

279
00:19:23,370 --> 00:19:24,288
I'm off.

280
00:19:25,330 --> 00:19:26,206
Bye.

281
00:19:26,290 --> 00:19:27,457
Thank you, Mr. Baek.

282
00:19:27,541 --> 00:19:29,501
Get in your car and go home. Hurry.

283
00:19:31,795 --> 00:19:32,838
Thank you!

284
00:19:44,266 --> 00:19:47,311
Eun-ho, you should go home too.

285
00:19:49,646 --> 00:19:51,940
That's a shame.
I wanted to talk a little longer.

286
00:19:55,819 --> 00:19:57,696
I've missed you all this time.

287
00:20:02,409 --> 00:20:04,036
But I should get going, right?

288
00:20:07,497 --> 00:20:09,833
-Let's talk more next time we meet.
-Yeah.

289
00:20:15,130 --> 00:20:15,964
Hey, punk!

290
00:20:16,048 --> 00:20:18,050
You always disappear
the second I look away.

291
00:20:19,134 --> 00:20:20,761
Hello, Ms. Na.

292
00:20:21,386 --> 00:20:24,139
There are many scary people
out there these days, you know.

293
00:20:24,223 --> 00:20:26,183
If this gets photographed, you're done.

294
00:20:26,266 --> 00:20:28,560
Stop giving Hee-chan a hard time
and just go.

295
00:20:29,645 --> 00:20:30,646
Get in the car.

296
00:20:30,729 --> 00:20:32,773
All right, I'm off. I'll call you.

297
00:20:32,856 --> 00:20:34,149
What for?

298
00:20:36,401 --> 00:20:37,236
I'll call you!

299
00:20:41,198 --> 00:20:42,658
-Bye.
-Bye!

300
00:20:45,285 --> 00:20:47,120
-Bye.
-Bye!

301
00:21:04,805 --> 00:21:05,889
There you are.

302
00:21:07,057 --> 00:21:10,602
Thanks to you,
I had to drive around the neighborhood.

303
00:21:11,103 --> 00:21:13,480
If he finds out we live together,
things could get awkward.

304
00:21:13,563 --> 00:21:15,190
Eun-ho might get the wrong idea.

305
00:21:15,274 --> 00:21:16,108
Why?

306
00:21:16,692 --> 00:21:17,943
Are you worried about him?

307
00:21:18,694 --> 00:21:21,738
Technically, we don't live together.
We live ten meters apart.

308
00:21:21,822 --> 00:21:25,575
It's still awkward.
You could say we live under the same roof.

309
00:21:26,493 --> 00:21:30,789
Eun-ho is such a sweet kid,
I'm sure he'd understand if I explained.

310
00:21:31,623 --> 00:21:33,083
Sweet, my ass.

311
00:21:33,166 --> 00:21:34,584
What's with you?

312
00:21:34,668 --> 00:21:37,296
He is sweet.
We've been friends since Wistful Youth.

313
00:21:37,379 --> 00:21:39,798
Men and women can never be just friends.

314
00:21:39,881 --> 00:21:41,717
And that wistful whatever.

315
00:21:41,800 --> 00:21:44,386
You're still going on about it?
It's been three years.

316
00:21:44,886 --> 00:21:47,014
Every time you two meet, you go on about…

317
00:21:47,097 --> 00:21:48,348
What did you say?

318
00:21:49,433 --> 00:21:51,059
No, I mean…

319
00:21:51,143 --> 00:21:53,687
I know it was your debut
and it meant a lot to you.

320
00:21:53,770 --> 00:21:54,604
Yeah.

321
00:21:54,688 --> 00:21:58,567
I've been floundering for three years.
That show means a lot to me.

322
00:21:59,443 --> 00:22:00,694
To you,

323
00:22:00,777 --> 00:22:05,365
it may be just another one-hour drama
no one knows about,

324
00:22:05,449 --> 00:22:07,492
but it means the world to me.

325
00:22:14,458 --> 00:22:15,751
I remember it too!

326
00:22:17,252 --> 00:22:18,712
Wistful Youth.

327
00:22:26,928 --> 00:22:28,597
Why is it such a big deal?

328
00:22:36,897 --> 00:22:38,607
You're a superstar.

329
00:22:38,690 --> 00:22:40,776
You should be careful
with everything you do.

330
00:22:40,859 --> 00:22:42,486
These days, everyone's a reporter.

331
00:22:42,569 --> 00:22:44,905
Everyone has a phone.
What if someone snaps a photo?

332
00:22:45,405 --> 00:22:47,324
I'm sick of repeating myself.

333
00:22:47,407 --> 00:22:48,241
Hee-chan.

334
00:22:49,701 --> 00:22:51,078
Should I just do the ad?

335
00:22:51,161 --> 00:22:52,287
What? Really?

336
00:22:52,871 --> 00:22:54,915
-Watch the road. You're going to crash.
-Okay.

337
00:22:55,791 --> 00:22:58,543
What made you come up with
such a thoughtful idea?

338
00:22:58,627 --> 00:23:01,713
Bo-bae and Mr. Baek Ho-rang
keep seeing each other

339
00:23:01,797 --> 00:23:03,298
because of work.

340
00:23:03,382 --> 00:23:06,218
Huh? Ms. Na is seeing Mr. Baek?

341
00:23:08,428 --> 00:23:10,138
If work brings us together again,

342
00:23:11,348 --> 00:23:13,517
we'll see each other more often, right?

343
00:23:13,600 --> 00:23:16,269
It'd be great
if you got to see the client more often.

344
00:23:16,853 --> 00:23:19,231
Man, Eun-ho has finally moved past
his artsy phase--

345
00:23:19,314 --> 00:23:20,357
Excuse me?

346
00:23:20,440 --> 00:23:23,693
I mean, you've changed your mind.
That's great.

347
00:23:34,913 --> 00:23:36,498
What made you call me first?

348
00:23:36,581 --> 00:23:37,582
Hey.

349
00:23:38,375 --> 00:23:40,168
I just wanted to see you.

350
00:23:40,710 --> 00:23:43,463
Did something bad happen
to my dear Seol-hee?

351
00:23:43,547 --> 00:23:45,257
Want me to entertain you a little?

352
00:23:46,049 --> 00:23:48,552
Do I look upset?
Actually, something good happened.

353
00:23:50,011 --> 00:23:50,971
Like what?

354
00:23:53,056 --> 00:23:56,101
I ran into Mr. Baek today,
and we had a little chat.

355
00:23:56,184 --> 00:23:57,018
Baek Ho-rang?

356
00:23:57,727 --> 00:23:58,562
Yeah.

357
00:23:59,312 --> 00:24:02,107
I knew he was kind,

358
00:24:02,607 --> 00:24:04,776
but he really looks after his staff,

359
00:24:04,860 --> 00:24:06,653
including his secretary.

360
00:24:07,446 --> 00:24:08,822
So that's why?

361
00:24:09,573 --> 00:24:11,825
The reason you're throwing
such a classy fit.

362
00:24:22,627 --> 00:24:24,087
You're right.

363
00:24:24,754 --> 00:24:27,424
Na Bo-bae. It was the secretary.

364
00:24:28,925 --> 00:24:31,178
The woman I saw at Baek Ho-rang's house.

365
00:24:34,598 --> 00:24:35,724
I see.

366
00:24:35,807 --> 00:24:38,602
He lives with another woman.
He doesn't even care about you.

367
00:24:38,685 --> 00:24:40,729
Why the hell are you still hung up on him?

368
00:24:50,071 --> 00:24:54,910
Baek Ho-rang is the only man
worthy of being my family.

369
00:25:07,631 --> 00:25:10,467
Kid! You can't run out like that!
You could've been killed.

370
00:25:10,550 --> 00:25:13,220
Why did you stop? Just run me over!

371
00:25:14,054 --> 00:25:17,140
Sir, I'm sorry. That girl won't move.

372
00:25:18,308 --> 00:25:19,142
Kid!

373
00:25:19,726 --> 00:25:20,727
Get lost.

374
00:25:29,444 --> 00:25:30,320
Think.

375
00:25:30,403 --> 00:25:33,490
Think of every way to protect yourself.

376
00:25:34,449 --> 00:25:36,826
Do your best to protect yourself.

377
00:25:36,910 --> 00:25:39,371
It's better than dying.

378
00:25:42,582 --> 00:25:47,462
I'm talking to you! Where are you going?
Han Seol-hee! Get back here!

379
00:26:07,524 --> 00:26:11,987
The best way to protect myself…

380
00:26:19,911 --> 00:26:23,915
Mr. Baek changed my life.

381
00:26:23,999 --> 00:26:25,792
What does he know about your life?

382
00:26:25,875 --> 00:26:27,043
I know more than he does.

383
00:26:27,961 --> 00:26:31,047
I know you're all twisted up inside.

384
00:26:32,090 --> 00:26:33,091
And so…

385
00:26:38,471 --> 00:26:39,889
So…

386
00:26:41,808 --> 00:26:42,809
Just

387
00:26:44,436 --> 00:26:45,645
come to me.

388
00:26:49,274 --> 00:26:50,191
Do-yoon.

389
00:26:51,192 --> 00:26:53,361
Two twisted people shouldn't be together.

390
00:27:02,787 --> 00:27:06,041
These will make the front pages
of the major newspapers next week.

391
00:27:06,708 --> 00:27:08,543
TS HOTEL CAUGHT EMBEZZLING 8 BILLION WON

392
00:27:09,085 --> 00:27:11,671
TS HOTEL EXECS PROBED
OVER 8-BILLION-WON EMBEZZLEMENT

393
00:27:14,132 --> 00:27:16,676
I guess they can use
that photo of Choi Do-yoon.

394
00:27:16,760 --> 00:27:19,429
The one of him drunk and swearing.
He looked good in it.

395
00:27:19,512 --> 00:27:21,640
Yes, sir. I'll let them know.

396
00:27:22,766 --> 00:27:23,975
We have to end it now.

397
00:27:25,769 --> 00:27:28,647
So that family
can't get in my way anymore.

398
00:27:29,147 --> 00:27:29,981
Yes, sir.

399
00:27:30,065 --> 00:27:32,817
What about the new face of our resort?
Still not finalized?

400
00:27:33,943 --> 00:27:35,028
I'm sorry, sir.

401
00:27:40,700 --> 00:27:41,576
Yes?

402
00:27:45,288 --> 00:27:48,458
Sir, Ji Eun-ho's agency called.

403
00:27:48,541 --> 00:27:51,002
They said he'll do the ad.

404
00:27:51,086 --> 00:27:51,920
Just like that?

405
00:27:52,003 --> 00:27:54,506
Yes. He'll be here in person soon.

406
00:27:54,589 --> 00:27:56,800
-Ji Eun-ho is coming here now?
-Yes.

407
00:27:56,883 --> 00:27:59,260
No way! I have to get a photo with him.

408
00:27:59,344 --> 00:28:01,429
No photos, Mr. Lee.

409
00:28:01,513 --> 00:28:03,390
Get a hold of yourself.

410
00:28:04,182 --> 00:28:07,560
Either way, this is great news for us!

411
00:28:07,644 --> 00:28:09,062
Well done, team.

412
00:28:09,145 --> 00:28:11,398
-High five!
-Yeah!

413
00:28:11,481 --> 00:28:13,066
-We did it!
-You too. High five!

414
00:28:14,359 --> 00:28:15,735
Well, I…

415
00:28:16,361 --> 00:28:18,279
I'm sorry. I got an urgent call.

416
00:28:18,363 --> 00:28:20,448
Yay!

417
00:28:22,617 --> 00:28:25,954
Bo-bae, do you want to try
writing a script?

418
00:28:26,037 --> 00:28:27,247
A short one.

419
00:28:29,165 --> 00:28:33,878
Actually, there's a director and writer
my actor wants to work with.

420
00:28:33,962 --> 00:28:36,631
Could we make working with them
part of the contract?

421
00:28:37,799 --> 00:28:41,052
He wants to choose
the director and writer?

422
00:28:41,136 --> 00:28:42,512
Could we do that?

423
00:28:43,221 --> 00:28:47,058
We'd have to sign
the director and writer too.

424
00:28:47,142 --> 00:28:48,518
We can't just bring in anyone.

425
00:28:48,601 --> 00:28:50,770
You probably know the director.

426
00:28:50,854 --> 00:28:52,897
Director Yeom Min-kyu. He directs dramas.

427
00:28:52,981 --> 00:28:54,566
Oh, Director Yeom.

428
00:28:55,066 --> 00:28:57,444
Well, he's well-known.

429
00:28:58,027 --> 00:28:59,112
And the writer?

430
00:28:59,195 --> 00:29:01,489
As for the writer…

431
00:29:02,449 --> 00:29:04,576
Mr. Baek would know better.

432
00:29:07,996 --> 00:29:08,913
Mr. Ji.

433
00:29:10,165 --> 00:29:13,293
Is this the reason
you wanted to sign the contract?

434
00:29:13,376 --> 00:29:14,252
Yes.

435
00:29:14,335 --> 00:29:16,880
Does the reason matter,
as long as we sign the contract?

436
00:29:18,882 --> 00:29:19,799
Mr. Baek.

437
00:29:20,300 --> 00:29:23,803
Is there some rule
against signing a contract

438
00:29:24,304 --> 00:29:25,346
for personal reasons?

439
00:29:33,062 --> 00:29:35,398
No. It's fine. Let's sign the contract.

440
00:29:35,482 --> 00:29:37,734
You, the director,

441
00:29:38,234 --> 00:29:39,444
and the writer.

442
00:29:39,527 --> 00:29:40,528
All three of you.

443
00:29:41,362 --> 00:29:42,655
Thank you.

444
00:29:45,408 --> 00:29:46,993
I look forward to it.

445
00:29:51,498 --> 00:29:53,875
I look forward to working with you.

446
00:30:12,519 --> 00:30:13,853
Why did you ask for me?

447
00:30:16,564 --> 00:30:17,732
Ms. Na Bo-bae.

448
00:30:19,609 --> 00:30:20,693
By any chance,

449
00:30:22,070 --> 00:30:24,948
did you ask Mr. Ji Eun-ho
to let you write the script?

450
00:30:25,532 --> 00:30:26,533
What?

451
00:30:26,616 --> 00:30:29,202
Mr. Ji said he'd do the ad

452
00:30:29,285 --> 00:30:32,831
on the condition
that you and Director Yeom work on it.

453
00:30:36,209 --> 00:30:38,878
Director Yeom is just an excuse.

454
00:30:38,962 --> 00:30:41,714
It's obvious
he just wants to work with you.

455
00:30:42,590 --> 00:30:45,677
Are you asking me if I used Eun-ho?

456
00:30:46,761 --> 00:30:47,595
Well…

457
00:30:49,013 --> 00:30:51,683
I did bring up Wistful Youth

458
00:30:52,183 --> 00:30:53,726
and said some harsh things last night…

459
00:30:54,644 --> 00:30:58,189
You two seem pretty close.
And you're running out of time.

460
00:30:58,273 --> 00:31:01,025
Your contract's up in two months.

461
00:31:01,526 --> 00:31:04,988
Wouldn't it be good for you
to have one more chance

462
00:31:05,071 --> 00:31:07,532
to show Director Yeom what you can do?

463
00:31:09,701 --> 00:31:11,452
Look, Mr. Baek Ho-rang.

464
00:31:11,995 --> 00:31:13,162
Sure.

465
00:31:13,246 --> 00:31:16,124
Maybe Eun-ho agreed to do the commercial
because of me.

466
00:31:16,207 --> 00:31:17,125
But you know,

467
00:31:17,709 --> 00:31:20,336
some people help and rely on each other
out of goodwill

468
00:31:20,420 --> 00:31:23,172
instead of using each other as tools.

469
00:31:23,256 --> 00:31:25,508
That's something you'll never understand.

470
00:31:28,052 --> 00:31:32,098
And I'd appreciate it
if you didn't summon me like this again.

471
00:31:32,181 --> 00:31:34,851
I mean, you have a fiancée.

472
00:31:34,934 --> 00:31:37,020
We don't want her getting the wrong idea.

473
00:31:37,103 --> 00:31:38,730
I told you I'm not getting married.

474
00:31:38,813 --> 00:31:40,523
-And about charging--
-Charging!

475
00:31:41,858 --> 00:31:44,777
We can charge just fine within ten meters.

476
00:31:54,412 --> 00:31:55,914
Why is she getting angry?

477
00:32:10,720 --> 00:32:13,640
You think Ms. Na and Mr. Baek are dating?

478
00:32:13,723 --> 00:32:15,433
They were arguing.

479
00:32:15,516 --> 00:32:18,227
She was even scolding Mr. Baek.

480
00:32:18,311 --> 00:32:19,479
No way!

481
00:32:19,562 --> 00:32:20,980
Seriously? That's crazy.

482
00:32:21,064 --> 00:32:23,274
Why else would a secretary scold
a senior managing director?

483
00:32:23,358 --> 00:32:25,401
They must be dating.

484
00:32:25,485 --> 00:32:28,029
-Gosh. That's a dead giveaway.
-Yeah, 100%.

485
00:32:28,112 --> 00:32:31,032
I'm telling you.
I heard them just as I was about to knock.

486
00:32:31,115 --> 00:32:31,950
-Oh my!
-My gosh!

487
00:32:32,033 --> 00:32:33,993
-So I stopped and listened.
-For real?

488
00:32:34,077 --> 00:32:35,119
This is insane.

489
00:32:35,203 --> 00:32:36,496
-I know, right?
-My gosh.

490
00:32:44,087 --> 00:32:45,546
This is the Executive Office.

491
00:32:45,630 --> 00:32:49,092
You know the list
of premium brand contacts we asked for?

492
00:32:49,175 --> 00:32:52,136
Please send it over right away so we can…

493
00:33:01,312 --> 00:33:04,941
Actually,
I saw something the other day too.

494
00:33:10,989 --> 00:33:12,907
WHAT ARE YOU UP TO, SEOL-HEE?

495
00:33:16,536 --> 00:33:17,996
Father!

496
00:33:18,830 --> 00:33:21,958
You nearly split your only son's head open
with that.

497
00:33:22,709 --> 00:33:26,879
Did you know Baek Ho-rang is preparing
to expose the embezzlement at TS Hotel?

498
00:33:27,380 --> 00:33:30,258
-Sorry?
-I bet you had no idea.

499
00:33:30,341 --> 00:33:34,846
Stop making yourself look dumber than him.

500
00:33:39,600 --> 00:33:40,852
TS HOTEL CAUGHT EMBEZZLING 8 BILLION WON

501
00:33:40,935 --> 00:33:43,021
If Reporter Park hadn't told me,

502
00:33:43,104 --> 00:33:45,815
that article would've run next week.

503
00:33:49,527 --> 00:33:52,196
If they find out what we did,

504
00:33:52,780 --> 00:33:54,991
your mother, you,

505
00:33:55,074 --> 00:33:56,200
and I

506
00:33:56,868 --> 00:33:58,369
are all done for.

507
00:34:04,042 --> 00:34:05,668
What was his name again?

508
00:34:06,461 --> 00:34:07,545
Your hotel's VP.

509
00:34:08,713 --> 00:34:10,173
It's Yoon Dong-seok.

510
00:34:10,256 --> 00:34:13,968
Yeah. Cut him loose.
Make sure it doesn't lead back to us.

511
00:34:16,179 --> 00:34:17,305
Better yet,

512
00:34:18,514 --> 00:34:21,142
just tie Baek Ho-rang to it
and get rid of them both.

513
00:34:21,893 --> 00:34:24,062
Fake a ledger or something.

514
00:34:24,145 --> 00:34:26,481
Make it look like
Baek Ho-rang had Yoon Dong-seok

515
00:34:26,564 --> 00:34:28,024
set up his own aunt and cousin.

516
00:34:28,107 --> 00:34:29,901
Something along those lines.

517
00:34:42,163 --> 00:34:45,958
Mr. Baek, this is Yoon Dong-seok,
the VP of TS Hotel.

518
00:34:52,298 --> 00:34:54,926
Thank you for making time for me, sir.

519
00:34:55,510 --> 00:34:56,344
First,

520
00:34:57,053 --> 00:34:58,012
let's have a drink.

521
00:34:59,013 --> 00:35:00,348
It's a bit early for alcohol.

522
00:35:02,433 --> 00:35:04,352
What did you want to talk to me about?

523
00:35:05,394 --> 00:35:06,896
Well…

524
00:35:51,149 --> 00:35:52,150
Ms. Na Bo-bae.

525
00:35:53,526 --> 00:35:55,111
Ms. Na. Over here.

526
00:36:08,082 --> 00:36:09,250
Thank you.

527
00:36:17,091 --> 00:36:20,803
You all remember what our new model,
Ji Eun-ho, asked for, right?

528
00:36:20,887 --> 00:36:24,056
Yes. He wanted to choose
the director and writer.

529
00:36:30,146 --> 00:36:34,817
Ms. Na Bo-bae over there is the writer.

530
00:36:36,152 --> 00:36:38,196
Hello, I'm Na Bo-bae.

531
00:36:38,279 --> 00:36:41,282
I used to be a drama writer.

532
00:36:41,365 --> 00:36:42,366
And now,

533
00:36:42,450 --> 00:36:45,536
as you know,
I'm Mr. Baek Ho-rang's secretary.

534
00:36:45,620 --> 00:36:48,873
Why would a drama writer become
a secretary?

535
00:36:49,790 --> 00:36:50,833
That's…

536
00:36:51,626 --> 00:36:52,793
Well…

537
00:37:00,092 --> 00:37:01,844
I was struggling financially.

538
00:37:04,430 --> 00:37:06,557
You see, as a drama writer,

539
00:37:06,641 --> 00:37:10,311
you don't get paid for your script
until the drama airs.

540
00:37:12,730 --> 00:37:13,856
Oh dear.

541
00:37:16,359 --> 00:37:19,820
I was starving to death,
with all my hopes and dreams gone.

542
00:37:21,364 --> 00:37:24,617
Then Mr. Baek Ho-rang offered me a job
as his secretary.

543
00:37:24,700 --> 00:37:27,411
So now I use my writing skills
as his secretary.

544
00:37:28,037 --> 00:37:33,960
Ms. Na has already worked
with Mr. Ji Eun-ho as writer and actor.

545
00:37:34,043 --> 00:37:35,920
She'll be a great help.

546
00:37:36,420 --> 00:37:39,715
She'll continue as my secretary,

547
00:37:39,799 --> 00:37:43,552
but for this project,
treat her as a writer.

548
00:37:45,596 --> 00:37:47,765
-Looking forward to working with you.
-Likewise.

549
00:37:48,266 --> 00:37:49,225
No wonder.

550
00:37:49,725 --> 00:37:52,728
The name was so unusual.
I thought it was someone by the same name.

551
00:37:53,437 --> 00:37:55,064
But it was you.

552
00:37:55,147 --> 00:37:56,983
Looking forward to working with you.

553
00:37:57,066 --> 00:37:59,110
I look forward to working with you too.

554
00:38:00,111 --> 00:38:04,198
Now, let's take a look at the concepts
you prepared.

555
00:38:04,824 --> 00:38:09,245
The key to the first concept
is the joy of eating.

556
00:38:09,328 --> 00:38:11,038
It's a gourmet-focused concept.

557
00:38:11,622 --> 00:38:14,125
It's not just about eating at the resort.

558
00:38:14,208 --> 00:38:16,002
It becomes the reason for the trip.

559
00:38:16,085 --> 00:38:17,336
Next.

560
00:38:17,420 --> 00:38:18,879
Gourmet food is important,

561
00:38:18,963 --> 00:38:21,173
but what comes to mind
when you think of "rest"?

562
00:38:21,257 --> 00:38:24,343
It's literally about resting
and doing nothing.

563
00:38:24,427 --> 00:38:25,469
Next.

564
00:38:25,553 --> 00:38:28,556
Next, we focused on the model, Ji Eun-ho.

565
00:38:28,639 --> 00:38:34,353
We thought the space where Ji Eun-ho rests
could become the resort's identity.

566
00:38:34,437 --> 00:38:35,938
That's all.

567
00:38:44,155 --> 00:38:46,907
Are these three concepts all you have?

568
00:38:46,991 --> 00:38:49,368
Yes. We were short on time.

569
00:38:49,452 --> 00:38:51,954
I see. Thank you all for your hard work.

570
00:38:53,080 --> 00:38:54,206
First,

571
00:38:55,207 --> 00:38:57,585
I think I should give you more time.

572
00:38:57,668 --> 00:39:00,338
Yes. Just give us one more week,
and we can--

573
00:39:00,421 --> 00:39:01,505
One day.

574
00:39:01,589 --> 00:39:02,590
Pardon?

575
00:39:05,593 --> 00:39:07,178
One day.

576
00:39:08,679 --> 00:39:14,185
Plan A was for Ms. Na
to turn today's meeting ideas

577
00:39:14,268 --> 00:39:16,437
into a one-minute drama.

578
00:39:16,520 --> 00:39:19,774
But since no one seems to have
any good ideas,

579
00:39:19,857 --> 00:39:21,275
we'll go with Plan B.

580
00:39:21,776 --> 00:39:24,403
We'll figure something out,
even if it takes all night.

581
00:39:25,279 --> 00:39:26,489
"All night"?

582
00:39:28,032 --> 00:39:29,909
Yes. Of course!

583
00:39:30,493 --> 00:39:32,453
My team loves pulling all-nighters.

584
00:39:33,746 --> 00:39:36,248
Glad to hear it. Let's work hard together.

585
00:39:36,332 --> 00:39:39,001
Mr. Baek, you're pulling an all-nighter
with the team?

586
00:39:39,085 --> 00:39:41,837
I figured this would happen,
so I cleared my schedule.

587
00:39:45,466 --> 00:39:46,467
Oh…

588
00:39:47,051 --> 00:39:48,302
You had it all planned out.

589
00:39:48,386 --> 00:39:49,637
As expected.

590
00:39:50,846 --> 00:39:52,431
Then I'll join you.

591
00:39:53,057 --> 00:39:56,018
Looks like we'll need plenty of coffee
and energy drinks tonight.

592
00:39:56,102 --> 00:39:57,395
-Then I'll--
-Ms. Na.

593
00:39:58,145 --> 00:40:00,564
I mean, Ms. Writer, you can head home.

594
00:40:01,315 --> 00:40:03,401
Hanlim should take care of this.

595
00:40:03,484 --> 00:40:06,612
Your job is to write the script.

596
00:40:58,956 --> 00:40:59,999
Ms. Na.

597
00:41:01,959 --> 00:41:02,793
Yes?

598
00:41:08,257 --> 00:41:10,176
I've been meaning to tell you this.

599
00:41:10,259 --> 00:41:13,929
I know you need to stay close
to Mr. Baek to charge him,

600
00:41:14,013 --> 00:41:16,390
but please be extra careful

601
00:41:16,474 --> 00:41:19,977
when Director Han Seol-hee
is at the office.

602
00:41:20,895 --> 00:41:22,229
Be careful?

603
00:41:22,313 --> 00:41:23,522
About what?

604
00:41:23,606 --> 00:41:27,109
Didn't you keep staring at Mr. Baek
during the meeting?

605
00:41:27,818 --> 00:41:31,697
That's because he was running the meeting.

606
00:41:31,780 --> 00:41:34,825
And you kept staring at him
on your way out.

607
00:41:34,909 --> 00:41:35,826
That was…

608
00:41:40,789 --> 00:41:41,749
I was glaring at him.

609
00:41:44,084 --> 00:41:45,419
In any case,

610
00:41:45,503 --> 00:41:50,883
Director Han is publicly known
as Mr. Baek's fiancée.

611
00:41:51,383 --> 00:41:56,347
So it'd be best not to make it so obvious
that you're close to Mr. Baek.

612
00:41:56,430 --> 00:41:58,432
I wasn't trying to make it obvious.

613
00:41:59,266 --> 00:42:01,352
We're actually close
because of the charging.

614
00:42:01,435 --> 00:42:04,605
Even so, I'd like you to be more careful.

615
00:42:04,688 --> 00:42:07,942
From his secretaries and employees
to the staff at his house,

616
00:42:08,025 --> 00:42:12,029
there are more eyes and ears
around Mr. Baek than you realize.

617
00:42:13,489 --> 00:42:16,116
And not all of them are on his side.

618
00:42:18,702 --> 00:42:19,537
Well, then.

619
00:42:26,210 --> 00:42:28,337
Why's he always picking on me?

620
00:42:29,755 --> 00:42:31,632
I should just zap him.

621
00:42:39,306 --> 00:42:41,684
Why didn't you tell me you were a writer?

622
00:42:41,767 --> 00:42:43,769
I had no idea.

623
00:42:44,353 --> 00:42:46,480
Now I can tell you're a writer.

624
00:42:46,564 --> 00:42:48,482
I can tell you're smart.

625
00:42:48,566 --> 00:42:50,818
What was the drama you did with Ji Eun-ho?

626
00:42:50,901 --> 00:42:52,945
It was just a single-episode drama.

627
00:42:53,028 --> 00:42:54,947
-I'm a secretary now.
-One-episode drama?

628
00:42:55,030 --> 00:42:56,574
-That's so cool.
-What's going on?

629
00:42:58,659 --> 00:43:02,496
If you don't want to pull an all-nighter
with Mr. Baek,

630
00:43:03,038 --> 00:43:05,374
you'd better focus on your work.

631
00:43:05,958 --> 00:43:07,126
-Yes, sir.
-Yes, sir.

632
00:43:07,209 --> 00:43:08,043
Tell me later.

633
00:43:09,044 --> 00:43:10,045
You're so cool.

634
00:43:22,641 --> 00:43:24,560
How am I supposed to charge him?

635
00:43:25,227 --> 00:43:28,939
He can be away from me for up to 25 hours,
so I guess it doesn't matter.

636
00:43:31,609 --> 00:43:33,402
Should I find something similar?

637
00:43:40,117 --> 00:43:43,662
He'll come to me if he needs me.
That's what Mr. Yoon said too.

638
00:44:08,520 --> 00:44:09,438
CHOI DO-YOON

639
00:44:12,441 --> 00:44:14,652
It's not a bad direction. I like it.

640
00:44:14,735 --> 00:44:18,530
Watching Ji Eun-ho act
could be part of the fun.

641
00:44:19,031 --> 00:44:20,532
Genre…

642
00:44:20,616 --> 00:44:21,950
CHOI DO-YOON SENT A PHOTO

643
00:44:22,034 --> 00:44:24,244
If there's a story,
it'll be more immersive.

644
00:44:39,301 --> 00:44:40,344
Hello?

645
00:44:40,427 --> 00:44:41,970
What was that photo you just sent?

646
00:44:42,054 --> 00:44:44,515
Your secretary seems to be going home
by herself today.

647
00:44:47,267 --> 00:44:48,352
Choi Do-yoon.

648
00:44:49,144 --> 00:44:50,354
Don't do anything stupid.

649
00:44:50,437 --> 00:44:51,897
How did you know, Ho-rang?

650
00:44:51,980 --> 00:44:53,982
I was just about to do something stupid.

651
00:44:54,066 --> 00:44:56,026
Hey, Choi Do-yoon.

652
00:44:58,529 --> 00:45:01,990
I was so curious
why you keep that woman around

653
00:45:02,074 --> 00:45:03,867
that I decided to find out for myself.

654
00:45:04,618 --> 00:45:06,954
I heard you were going to be
in a meeting all night.

655
00:45:07,871 --> 00:45:08,956
Good luck.

656
00:45:55,043 --> 00:45:56,420
PORTABLE CHARGER

657
00:45:57,254 --> 00:45:58,547
Ms. Na Bo-bae.

658
00:46:00,340 --> 00:46:01,675
Where are you right now?

659
00:46:02,301 --> 00:46:03,510
Are you okay?

660
00:46:03,594 --> 00:46:04,636
Sorry?

661
00:46:05,220 --> 00:46:06,597
I'm at the office.

662
00:46:24,198 --> 00:46:26,033
What's wrong? You look pale.

663
00:46:26,116 --> 00:46:27,868
Earlier, why didn't you…

664
00:46:29,077 --> 00:46:30,829
Why didn't you pick up your phone?

665
00:46:30,913 --> 00:46:34,374
I was talking to my friend, Seo-jeong.

666
00:46:34,875 --> 00:46:36,960
But why do you look like that?

667
00:46:37,044 --> 00:46:38,587
What's wrong? Are you sick?

668
00:46:38,670 --> 00:46:39,797
No.

669
00:46:41,548 --> 00:46:43,467
Never mind. Let's talk somewhere else.

670
00:46:44,760 --> 00:46:45,594
But…

671
00:46:48,889 --> 00:46:51,266
Why were you looking for me?
Is your heart okay?

672
00:46:51,350 --> 00:46:53,143
Come on. Tell me.

673
00:46:53,227 --> 00:46:56,438
No, it's not about charging…

674
00:46:57,105 --> 00:46:57,940
It's…

675
00:46:58,649 --> 00:46:59,650
Did anything happen

676
00:47:00,776 --> 00:47:01,985
with Choi Do-yoon?

677
00:47:03,862 --> 00:47:04,696
Well…

678
00:47:06,365 --> 00:47:07,616
Did he try to hurt you?

679
00:47:07,699 --> 00:47:09,076
You mean your cousin?

680
00:47:09,159 --> 00:47:11,703
I did run into him earlier
at the bus stop.

681
00:47:12,955 --> 00:47:15,499
Hey, Ms. Na Bo-bae. It's been a while.

682
00:47:20,587 --> 00:47:22,965
You're Mr. Baek Ho-rang's cousin.

683
00:47:23,757 --> 00:47:25,467
Are you going home? Want a ride?

684
00:47:25,551 --> 00:47:26,802
No, thanks.

685
00:47:28,262 --> 00:47:30,138
I like girls who play hard to get.

686
00:47:42,568 --> 00:47:43,902
Do you want to grab a drink?

687
00:47:45,571 --> 00:47:47,447
We can have a deep conversation.

688
00:47:53,495 --> 00:47:54,496
Hello?

689
00:47:55,080 --> 00:47:56,164
Hey, Seo-jeong.

690
00:47:57,624 --> 00:47:59,626
Really? You're coming to the resort?

691
00:48:00,252 --> 00:48:02,921
Yeah. Call me
after you drop Director Yeom off.

692
00:48:03,422 --> 00:48:04,256
All right.

693
00:48:09,011 --> 00:48:13,473
I just made plans with someone else,
so I can't drink with you.

694
00:48:13,974 --> 00:48:17,686
Honestly, I don't even want
a shallow conversation with you.

695
00:48:18,270 --> 00:48:19,688
That's a shame.

696
00:48:19,771 --> 00:48:21,231
Not for me.

697
00:48:22,566 --> 00:48:24,276
Get going. Yeah.

698
00:48:32,200 --> 00:48:33,076
That stings!

699
00:48:34,369 --> 00:48:35,203
What was that?

700
00:48:38,040 --> 00:48:38,999
Bye!

701
00:48:49,885 --> 00:48:51,553
She's kind of cute, huh?

702
00:48:52,554 --> 00:48:54,014
Damn.

703
00:48:57,267 --> 00:48:58,268
What?

704
00:48:59,227 --> 00:49:00,145
What's wrong with this car?

705
00:49:02,147 --> 00:49:03,649
Damn it.

706
00:49:03,732 --> 00:49:05,776
Was that really all?

707
00:49:05,859 --> 00:49:08,362
Yeah. Then I came back to the office
to meet my friend.

708
00:49:12,491 --> 00:49:13,700
Your friend? Which one?

709
00:49:13,784 --> 00:49:14,826
Why do you ask?

710
00:49:14,910 --> 00:49:17,663
Do you think I'd meet Eun-ho
and plot behind your back?

711
00:49:18,497 --> 00:49:22,668
Who I meet is none of your business.
If you don't need charging, I'm leaving.

712
00:49:29,675 --> 00:49:30,550
What are you doing?

713
00:49:35,347 --> 00:49:37,516
Let go! You'll rip my clothes!

714
00:49:39,726 --> 00:49:41,395
Ms. Na Bo-bae.

715
00:49:42,479 --> 00:49:44,982
Can't you cancel your plans for today?

716
00:49:46,024 --> 00:49:46,858
Huh?

717
00:49:47,609 --> 00:49:49,319
I'm just worried!

718
00:49:49,861 --> 00:49:50,946
About my health!

719
00:49:51,029 --> 00:49:54,825
I'm not feeling well,
and my battery's running low!

720
00:49:54,908 --> 00:49:57,244
What? So you're not feeling well.

721
00:49:57,327 --> 00:49:59,287
You need a supercharge right now,
don't you?

722
00:49:59,371 --> 00:50:02,332
No, I don't need a supercharge.

723
00:50:05,168 --> 00:50:06,420
Can't you just

724
00:50:07,004 --> 00:50:09,756
stay with me during my meeting?

725
00:50:09,840 --> 00:50:12,426
You said you didn't need me
during your meeting.

726
00:50:14,302 --> 00:50:15,762
Just be honest with me.

727
00:50:16,346 --> 00:50:17,597
Are you sick?

728
00:50:20,976 --> 00:50:23,478
I feel sick, but maybe I don't.

729
00:50:25,897 --> 00:50:27,482
Let's charge you first.

730
00:50:27,566 --> 00:50:29,192
There's no one else here now.

731
00:50:30,360 --> 00:50:31,570
You can talk now.

732
00:50:33,989 --> 00:50:34,906
Yes.

733
00:50:34,990 --> 00:50:36,074
Hold on a second.

734
00:50:40,245 --> 00:50:41,872
That's Mr. Yoon, isn't it?

735
00:50:41,955 --> 00:50:43,165
Yes.

736
00:50:43,749 --> 00:50:45,125
I think it's him.

737
00:50:45,208 --> 00:50:46,585
I think he's on the phone.

738
00:50:52,174 --> 00:50:53,425
Damn it.

739
00:50:53,508 --> 00:50:56,720
If he finds out I'm with you,
he'll give me an earful again.

740
00:50:59,681 --> 00:51:00,599
Follow me.

741
00:51:15,530 --> 00:51:17,365
I don't think anyone's here.

742
00:51:17,449 --> 00:51:19,868
Come on. Let's charge you
before anyone shows up.

743
00:51:20,660 --> 00:51:22,954
Hey, wait a second.

744
00:51:24,372 --> 00:51:26,625
I didn't ask you to stay to charge me.

745
00:51:27,209 --> 00:51:28,585
Actually…

746
00:51:30,879 --> 00:51:32,589
Choi Do-yoon threatened me.

747
00:51:32,672 --> 00:51:35,008
He said he'd do something to you.

748
00:51:36,051 --> 00:51:37,636
I was worried about that.

749
00:51:38,512 --> 00:51:39,471
Threatened you?

750
00:51:42,933 --> 00:51:44,601
But he didn't do anything to me.

751
00:51:44,684 --> 00:51:46,186
We talked for maybe a minute.

752
00:51:46,770 --> 00:51:48,271
Well, you never know.

753
00:51:48,355 --> 00:51:52,609
Do-yoon has always been determined
to find my weaknesses.

754
00:51:55,028 --> 00:51:57,531
But he can't do anything to me.

755
00:51:57,614 --> 00:51:59,574
What? How can you be so sure?

756
00:52:01,326 --> 00:52:02,160
Well…

757
00:52:03,995 --> 00:52:06,581
If he touches me,
he'll end up like a rotisserie chicken.

758
00:52:07,332 --> 00:52:09,668
I told you
my brother and sister were athletes.

759
00:52:09,751 --> 00:52:11,795
I learned some self-defense.

760
00:52:11,878 --> 00:52:14,339
I've never lost a fight with anyone.

761
00:52:14,422 --> 00:52:15,715
Don't worry.

762
00:52:16,758 --> 00:52:20,178
Gosh, you worry too much.

763
00:52:20,804 --> 00:52:23,181
Come on.
I'll fully charge you before I go.

764
00:52:26,226 --> 00:52:27,060
Oh man.

765
00:52:44,578 --> 00:52:45,620
Girlfriend?

766
00:52:46,329 --> 00:52:47,956
Isn't that Director Han Seol-hee?

767
00:52:48,456 --> 00:52:49,583
They're in the meeting.

768
00:52:50,083 --> 00:52:52,919
I heard from the secretaries

769
00:52:53,003 --> 00:52:56,006
that Mr. Baek was dating
our project writer.

770
00:52:56,089 --> 00:52:57,799
You know, the secretary.

771
00:52:57,883 --> 00:52:59,009
What?

772
00:52:59,593 --> 00:53:04,639
They didn't even start dating
until after the wedding announcement.

773
00:53:05,307 --> 00:53:06,641
Isn't that practically an affair?

774
00:53:06,725 --> 00:53:08,935
-Of course it is.
-Is that what it is?

775
00:53:09,519 --> 00:53:11,271
-Yes.
-I didn't think he was like that.

776
00:53:18,987 --> 00:53:20,614
Director Han. Hello.

777
00:53:20,697 --> 00:53:22,240
-Hello, sir. You made it.
-Yes.

778
00:53:22,324 --> 00:53:24,117
Sorry for calling you so late.
We're short on time.

779
00:53:24,201 --> 00:53:26,203
Pulling an all-nighter is nothing
in showbiz.

780
00:53:26,286 --> 00:53:27,370
Where's Ho-rang?

781
00:53:27,454 --> 00:53:28,747
He called his senior here.

782
00:53:28,830 --> 00:53:31,249
He should be the one coming out
to greet me, right?

783
00:53:31,333 --> 00:53:33,627
-One moment. I'll give him a call.
-Sure.

784
00:53:34,711 --> 00:53:35,921
-This way.
-Sure.

785
00:53:51,436 --> 00:53:52,479
That startled me.

786
00:53:55,398 --> 00:53:56,733
DIRECTOR HAN SEOL-HEE

787
00:53:56,816 --> 00:53:59,569
Didn't you just hear
a phone vibrating in here?

788
00:54:01,071 --> 00:54:03,531
If we get caught here,
it'll look suspicious.

789
00:54:03,615 --> 00:54:05,075
-What now?
-Huh?

790
00:54:05,158 --> 00:54:06,409
Is he in here?

791
00:54:07,911 --> 00:54:08,745
Ho-rang.

792
00:54:08,828 --> 00:54:09,663
Shoot.

793
00:54:17,003 --> 00:54:19,214
-Come here! Hurry!
-What are you doing there?

794
00:54:19,297 --> 00:54:20,715
Come on, hurry!

795
00:54:29,391 --> 00:54:30,642
Get in here, quick!

796
00:54:33,186 --> 00:54:34,229
Oh man.

797
00:54:34,312 --> 00:54:35,313
Ho-rang?

798
00:54:37,274 --> 00:54:38,316
Ho-rang.

799
00:54:40,277 --> 00:54:41,361
The door's locked.

800
00:54:43,196 --> 00:54:45,740
You can only lock this door
from the inside.

801
00:54:46,533 --> 00:54:48,159
That means he's inside right now.

802
00:54:49,286 --> 00:54:50,328
You sleeping in there?

803
00:54:51,579 --> 00:54:54,082
You called me here,
and you're sleeping in there?

804
00:54:54,749 --> 00:54:55,792
Hey, wake up.

805
00:54:56,584 --> 00:54:57,419
Ho-rang!

806
00:54:58,420 --> 00:55:00,839
Wake up, or I break the door down.
That's my Plan B.

807
00:55:00,922 --> 00:55:02,299
Wake up before that happens.

808
00:55:03,633 --> 00:55:04,467
All right?

809
00:55:08,888 --> 00:55:10,056
Turn it off.

810
00:55:10,140 --> 00:55:11,224
-Turn it off.
-Okay.

811
00:55:11,725 --> 00:55:14,144
I think I heard something.

812
00:55:14,769 --> 00:55:16,313
-You heard that too, right?
-Yes.

813
00:55:16,396 --> 00:55:17,605
You did, right?

814
00:55:20,692 --> 00:55:21,651
Ho-rang.

815
00:55:22,444 --> 00:55:23,278
Director Yeom?

816
00:55:24,195 --> 00:55:26,281
-Director Han.
-You're Mr. Baek's secretary.

817
00:55:26,364 --> 00:55:29,159
I think Mr. Baek's in there.
Could you roar like a tiger?

818
00:55:29,784 --> 00:55:30,618
Excuse me?

819
00:55:31,328 --> 00:55:32,162
Just kidding.

820
00:55:32,245 --> 00:55:33,079
I'll do it.

821
00:55:33,163 --> 00:55:35,373
Mr. Yoon, do you have a master key?

822
00:55:36,207 --> 00:55:38,501
The master key should be in my desk.

823
00:55:39,002 --> 00:55:39,836
Why do you ask?

824
00:55:43,548 --> 00:55:44,549
Got it.

825
00:55:58,605 --> 00:55:59,606
Quiet.

826
00:56:24,047 --> 00:56:25,715
See? Look at that.

827
00:56:30,887 --> 00:56:33,306
Mr. Baek. Please give us one more week.

828
00:56:33,390 --> 00:56:34,474
It's not him.

829
00:56:35,100 --> 00:56:36,101
Who is that?

830
00:56:38,019 --> 00:56:39,646
Gosh, he must be really tired.

831
00:56:39,729 --> 00:56:40,730
Sir.

832
00:56:43,858 --> 00:56:46,236
Tell him to come to the meeting room
once he's up.

833
00:56:49,322 --> 00:56:50,365
I'm off too.

834
00:57:21,813 --> 00:57:23,815
Where is this punk?

835
00:57:23,898 --> 00:57:26,401
How dare he keep me waiting?
I'm Yeom Min-kyu.

836
00:57:27,819 --> 00:57:29,654
He's gone.

837
00:57:31,698 --> 00:57:33,700
I thought my heart was going to explode.

838
00:57:42,375 --> 00:57:43,668
Ms. Na Bo-bae.

839
00:57:45,795 --> 00:57:46,629
Yes?

840
00:57:48,590 --> 00:57:49,757
Me too.

841
00:57:53,052 --> 00:57:54,262
What do you mean?

842
00:57:55,472 --> 00:57:56,598
When I'm

843
00:57:57,307 --> 00:57:59,434
with you,

844
00:58:00,602 --> 00:58:02,812
I worry about you all the time.

845
00:58:03,480 --> 00:58:05,190
My heart's racing so fast…

846
00:58:09,402 --> 00:58:11,029
it feels like it will explode.

847
01:00:06,477 --> 01:00:11,107
Subtitle translation by: Sung In Jang
